{"name":"Liberty Bell Grey","hex":"#696b6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"liberty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition of being free.","The condition of being free from imprisonment, slavery or forced labour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberty"},{"term":"bell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive instrument made of metal or other hard material, typically but not always in the shape of an inverted cup with a flared rim, which resonates when struck.","An instrument that emits a ringing sound, situated on a bicycle's handlebar and used by the cyclist to warn of their presence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attach a bell to.","To shape so that it flares out like a bell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Liberty Bell","blocks":[{"text":"The Liberty Bell, previously called the State House Bell or Old State House Bell, is an iconic symbol of American independence, located in Philadelphia. It was first called the Liberty Bell by members of the American abolitionist movement, who used it as a symbol. Originally placed in the steeple of the Pennsylvania State House, the Liberty Bell today is located across the street from Independence Hall in the Liberty Bell Center in Independence National Historical Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Liberty_Bell_2017a.jpg/330px-Liberty_Bell_2017a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberty_Bell","wikidata":"Q390306"},{"title":"Liberty","blocks":[{"text":"Liberty is the state of being free within society from restrictions imposed by authority on one's way of life, behavior, or political views. The concept of liberty can vary depending on perspective and context. In the constitutional law of the United States, ordered liberty means creating a balanced society where individuals have the freedom to act without unnecessary interference and access to opportunities and resources to pursue their goals, all within a fair legal system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Statue_of_Liberty_7.jpg/330px-Statue_of_Liberty_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberty","wikidata":"Q2979"},{"title":"Bell","blocks":[{"text":"A bell is a directly struck idiophone percussion instrument. Most bells have the shape of a hollow cup that—when struck—vibrates in a single strong strike tone, with its sides forming an efficient resonator. The strike may be made by an internal \"clapper\" or \"uvula\", an external hammer, or—in small bells—by a small loose sphere enclosed within the body of the bell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Parts_of_a_Bell.svg/330px-Parts_of_a_Bell.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell","wikidata":"Q101401"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Exterior_view_of_Independence_Hall_%28circa_1770s%29.jpg/330px-Exterior_view_of_Independence_Hall_%28circa_1770s%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Exterior_view_of_Independence_Hall_%28circa_1770s%29.jpg/330px-Exterior_view_of_Independence_Hall_%28circa_1770s%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration of the Pennsylvania State House, later renamed Independence Hall, as it appeared in the 1770s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AExterior_view_of_Independence_Hall_(circa_1770s).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg/500px-2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg/1280px-2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg/500px-2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zion United Church of Christ in Allentown, Pennsylvania, where the Liberty Bell was hidden under floor boards during the British occupation of Philadelphia during the Revolutionary War","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2011_-_Zion_Reformed_Church.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bellringer1776.jpg/330px-Bellringer1776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bellringer1776.jpg/330px-Bellringer1776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bellman Informed of the Passage of the Declaration of Independence, an 1854 illustration of th